which is Latin for I'll suck nothing.

273
00:12:56,730 --> 00:12:57,930
Of course I'm joking

274
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,660
because the Latin for that is nihil exsorbibo.

275
00:13:00,730 --> 00:13:03,160
That is not Toby,

276
00:13:03,230 --> 00:13:04,260
this is Toby.

277
00:13:04,330 --> 00:13:06,000
Raj, what do you think?

278
00:13:06,030 --> 00:13:08,860
Oh, I really don't care anymore.

279
00:13:10,230 --> 00:13:12,960
God, I had the most horrible night.

280
00:13:14,330 --> 00:13:17,330
Obviously another carnal fiasco with the shiksi goddess.

281
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,100
Shiksa. Shik-sa.

282
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,260
Forgive me.

283
00:13:21,330 --> 00:13:24,260
Yiddish was not spoken in East Texas.

284
00:13:24,330 --> 00:13:27,600
And if it was, it wasn't spoken for long.

285
00:13:27,660 --> 00:13:28,760
Yeah, fine, whatever.

286
00:13:28,830 --> 00:13:30,800
The point is, you're wrong again.

287
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:33,260
We haven't established that I'm wrong once. All right.

288
00:13:33,330 --> 00:13:34,500
Tell you what. Let's go down

289
00:13:34,530 --> 00:13:36,000
to the Entomology Department

290
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:37,330
and let Professor Crawley tell us

291
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,230
what kind of cricket Toby is.

292
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:40,500
He's a snowy tree cricket,

293
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:42,200
and his name is Jiminy.

294
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:45,160
I bet I could throw a rock in this room

295
00:13:45,230 --> 00:13:47,730
and come up with three better friends.

296
00:13:54,730 --> 00:13:57,530
Holy crap.

297
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:04,630
It's like Silence of the Lambs down here.

298
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,400
Don't do that.

299
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,400
You're such a girl.

300
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:14,500
The're just bugs.

301
00:14:14,530 --> 00:14:15,930
Yeah, well, I don't like bugs, okay?

302
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,060
They freak me out.

303
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,430
Interesting

304
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,800
You're afraid of insects and women.

305
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:24,330
Ladybugs must render you catatonic.

306
00:14:25,830 --> 00:14:28,760
It was a joke.

307
00:14:28,830 --> 00:14:31,430
I made it to lessen your discomfort.

308
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:34,000
You're welcome.

309
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:40,600
Don't knock.

310
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:41,860
Just walk in.

311
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,560
Why be polite to the world's leading expert

312
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,600
on the dung beetle?

313
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:48,260
Excuse me,

314
00:14:48,330 --> 00:14:50,000
are you Professor Crawley?

315
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:52,100
Who wants to know?

316
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:55,600
I'm Dr. Cooper from the Physics Department.

317
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:57,260
Couldn't wait, huh?

318
00:14:57,260 --> 00:14:58,330
I'm sorry?

319
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,800
I haven't even packed yet,

320
00:14:59,830 --> 00:15:01,860
and you're already measuring my lab

321
00:15:01,930 --> 00:15:06,160
for one of your godless laser machines.

322
00:15:06,230 --> 00:15:08,230
No, you don't understand.

323
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:09,830
We just want to ask you a question.

324
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:12,830
Let me ask you one first.

325
00:15:12,860 --> 00:15:14,860
What's a world renowned entomologist

326
00:15:14,930 --> 00:15:16,530
with a doctorate

327
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:19,100
and 20 years of experience to do with his life

328
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:22,600
when the university cuts off the funding for his lab, huh?

329
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:24,630
Ask rhetorical questions

330
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:27,300
that make people uncomfortable?

331
00:15:29,630 --> 00:15:32,000
What's your deal?

332
00:15:32,030 --> 00:15:35,700
Are they planning to outsource my job to Bangalore?

333
00:15:37,030 --> 00:15:39,730
I'm from New Delhi.

334
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:41,730
Maybe you should find another entomologist.

335
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,500
No, no. We're here. Let's settle this.

336
00:15:43,530 --> 00:15:46,330
Professor, can you identify our cricket?

337
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,760
Of course I can.

338
00:15:47,830 --> 00:15:51,430
I can identify every insect and arachnid on the planet.

339
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:52,900
Not that that's going

340
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:56,230
to keep me from having to move in with my daughter in Oxnard.

341
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:57,730
And we're not talking

342
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,260
Oxnard at the beach. No!

343
00:16:00,330 --> 00:16:01,530
We're talking Oxnard

344
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:04,560
in the onion fields.

345
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:09,800
Well, could you look at Toby?

346
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:11,300
Toby?

347
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:15,360
What a stupid name for a cricket.

348
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,360
Told ya.

349
00:16:18,430 --> 00:16:20,060
It's a field cricket.

350
00:16:20,130 --> 00:16:21,300
- Yes! - No, no, wait.

351
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:23,300
Dr. Crawley, are you sure?

352
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:27,030
Young man,I've been studying insects since I was eight years old.

353
00:16:27,060 --> 00:16:29,930
You know what they used to call me in school?

354
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,960
Creepy Crawley.

355
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:33,860
Cruel as that may be,

356
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,960
But this is not in itself a credential.

357
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,260
Let me show you something.

358
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,930
See that?

359
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,100
That's a Crawley's dung beetle.

360
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:45,730
I discovered it after spending six months slogging

361
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,760
Through a Bornean rain forest,

362
00:16:47,830 --> 00:16:52,960
While my wife was back home shacking up with a two-bit ornithologist

363
00:16:53,030 --> 00:16:57,730
Who lives on a sailboat and likes to wear boot-cut jeans!

364
00:16:57,800 --> 00:17:03,330
So, when I tell you that it's a common field cricket,

365
00:17:03,330 --> 00:17:05,900
You can take that to the damn bank!

366
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:07,700
'Cause God knows I can't!

367
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:10,500
That tramp took me for everything!

368
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:18,630
Well, apparently, I was wrong.

369
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,700
Congratulations.

370
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:28,760
Enjoy Oxnard.

371
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:33,160
I'm sure your daughter's looking forward to having you.

372
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,070
Oh, hey, Sheldon.

373
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:43,900
What you got there? New comic book?

374
00:17:43,970 --> 00:17:46,030
Old comic book.

375
00:17:46,070 --> 00:17:49,030
I just retrieved it from my safe deposit box.

376
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:52,070
What do you have a safe deposit box for?

377
00:17:52,130 --> 00:17:55,070
Old comic books.

378
00:17:55,100 --> 00:18:00,230
I lost this to Wolowitz in an ill-considered cricket wager.

379
00:18:00,270 --> 00:18:02,930
What, do they have Wii cricket now?

380
00:18:04,370 --> 00:18:06,430
That can't be very popular.

381
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,630
Penny, I'd rather not talk about it.

382
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:10,300
Well, if it makes you feel any better,

383
00:18:10,370 --> 00:18:11,800
I'm not feeling so hot either.

384
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:15,430
Why would that make me feel better?

385
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:18,000
I don't know, empathy?

386
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:24,100
Anyway, I'm just saying,

387
00:18:24,130 --> 00:18:26,100
That you're feeling upset about something with Howard,

388
00:18:26,130 --> 00:18:27,930
- And I'm upset about something with Leonard. - Yes

389
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,130
Yes, the disappointing sex.

390
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:32,400
That's an inexact parallel.

391
00:18:32,470 --> 00:18:35,030
You and Leonard can always return to being friends,

392
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:36,570
Whereas I can never return to a state

393
00:18:36,630 --> 00:18:39,020
In which Wolowitz has not bested me

394
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:41,400
Like Mrs. Riley's chicken.

395
00:18:41,430 --> 00:18:43,530
What's Mrs. Riley's chicken?

396
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:46,600
A chicken that was owned by Mrs. Riley.

397
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:49,500
Okay, forget the chicken.

398
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,900
Well, I wish I could.

399
00:18:51,930 --> 00:18:53,500
No, no.

400
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,330
You may be right about me and Leonard.

401
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,670
Of course I'm right.

402
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:59,500
What are the odds I'd be wrong twice in one week?

403
00:18:59,570 --> 00:19:01,870
No, I mean, we can always go back to being friends.

404
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:03,970
I just said that.

405
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,500
This conversation has started to circle.Meeting adjourned.

406
00:19:13,530 --> 00:19:15,970
What's going on?

407
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:19,070
Oh,you'd like to catch up on the events of the day. All right

408
00:19:19,130 --> 00:19:21,600
Well, there was a half-hour wait at the bank

409
00:19:21,670 --> 00:19:23,200
To get into my safe deposit box,

410
00:19:23,230 --> 00:19:25,900
I was forced to talk to Penny about your sexual problems,

411
00:19:25,970 --> 00:19:27,370
And, oh, yes,

412
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,370
In a moment filled with biblical resonance,

413
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,430
Pride wentth before my fall,

414
00:19:31,430 --> 00:19:35,230
Causing my Flash 123 to go with to Wolowitz.

415
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:36,470
Wait a minute.

416
00:19:36,530 --> 00:19:39,030
You talked to Penny about our sex life?

417
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:42,870
Leonard,it astonishes me how you continually fixate on the trivial.

418
00:19:42,930 --> 00:19:45,670
I lost a bet to Wolowitz.

419
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:47,000
Right, right.

420
00:19:47,030 --> 00:19:48,600
You're saying you talked to Penny?

421
00:19:48,670 --> 00:19:49,930
Ye-Yes.

422
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:50,670
Interesting.

423
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:52,500
Hardly.

424
00:19:52,570 --> 00:19:53,630
Excuse me.

425
00:19:53,670 --> 00:19:56,100
Have I crossed some sort of line again?

426
00:19:56,170 --> 00:19:58,130
Little bit.

427
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,200
Oh, who cares?

428
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,160
Uh, what did Sheldon say to you?

429
00:20:16,230 --> 00:20:17,200
Not a lot.

430
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:20,600
Just that we always have the option of going back to being friends.

431
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:22,760
Is that what you want?

432
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:24,060
I don't know.

433
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,730
I mean, you have to admit

434
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:28,460
Things seemed simpler when we were just friends.

435
00:20:28,530 --> 00:20:30,330
I guess.

436
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,960
It would take the pressure off.

437
00:20:32,030 --> 00:20:34,260
It would, wouldn't it?

438
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:37,460
So, we'll just be friends.

439
00:20:37,530 --> 00:20:38,630
Good.

440
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:40,060
Good.

441
00:20:40,130 --> 00:20:42,060
Come here.

442
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:57,430
Okay-dokay.

